# oracle: compute rattlers/atom type (contacts within the lj cutoff 1.5, a rattler has fewer than 3 contacts, up to 10 tries) on a fluid of 108 lj atoms (fcc 0.8442, velocity create 0.3), 10 steps of nve; the rattler flags are dumped at step 10 and their count is in thermo
# oracle: native: b332f28 (installed lmp; compute rattlers/atom is in the EXTRA-COMPUTE package of that binary)
# oracle-files: w227xc_rattlers.dump
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=none filerel=1e-12
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (thermo rows, final atoms): thermo 3.2e-16, atoms n/a (atoms=none; the rattler flags are the dump file, worst token 0).
units           lj
atom_style      atomic
lattice         fcc 0.8442
region          box block 0 3 0 3 0 3
create_box      1 box
create_atoms    1 box
mass            1 1.0
velocity        all create 0.3 4242 loop geom
pair_style      lj/cut 1.5
pair_coeff      1 1 1.0 1.0 1.5
compute         rat all rattlers/atom type 3 10
dump            d1 all custom 10 w227xc_rattlers.dump id c_rat
dump_modify     d1 sort id format float %.15g
fix             1 all nve
thermo_style    custom step pe c_rat
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          10
run             10
